<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <!-- App Sandbox is deliberately OFF. The desktop media pipeline spawns ffmpeg as a
         child process against user-picked files, and a sandboxed child does not inherit
         the security-scoped file grant — the pipeline cannot work sandboxed. Castmill
         Desktop distributes as a notarized pkg outside the Mac App Store (roadmap E10.4),
         which does not require the sandbox. Revisit ONLY if MAS distribution is wanted,
         which would mean bundling ffmpeg as a signed helper or linking libav in-process. -->
    <!-- NO keychain-access-groups here, on purpose — twice burned:
         1. Without it, MAUI SecureStorage throws on every call on Mac Catalyst, so the
            refresh token was never persisted and sessions died 15 minutes after sign-in.
         2. WITH it, an ad-hoc-signed Debug build (this machine has zero codesigning
            identities) is killed by launchd at spawn — keychain-access-groups is a
            RESTRICTED entitlement that requires a provisioning profile to validate
            (RBSRequestErrorDomain Code=5, "Launchd job spawn failed").
         So dev builds run without the Keychain and DesktopTokenProvider falls back to a
         user-only (0600) file for restart survival; live sessions never depend on storage
         at all (memory-authoritative, frontend ADR-F27). Add the entitlement back ONLY
         together with real signing — i.e. in the notarized-pkg packaging step (E10.4),
         where SecureStorage then takes over from the file automatically. -->
    <dict>
    </dict>
</plist>
